# Extraction stub — arXiv:1907.02359

**Status:** placeholder. Prose extraction for this replication was performed with `pdftotext` (see `work/paper.txt`, 2261 lines) rather than nougat. Equations were transcribed by hand from the PDF where needed for the QAOA implementation (see `code/qaoa_maxcut.py` for the concrete Ising-Hamiltonian / mixer encoding of Willsch Eqs. 12–14).

To regenerate as MMD with `nougat` (free, GPU-optional):

```
pip install nougat-ocr
nougat work/paper.pdf --out extraction/ --markdown
# writes extraction/paper.mmd (or similarly named); rename/move to nougat.mmd
```

Nougat rendering was not required for the verdict on this paper because:
1. All numeric claims used in the replication (approximation-ratio curves, Farhi 0.6924 bound, monotone-p trend) are text-narrative claims plus small tables, all captured cleanly in `work/paper.txt`.
2. The equations we needed to reimplement (cost unitary $e^{-i\gamma H_C}$ with $H_C = \sum_{(i,j)}\tfrac{1}{2}(Z_i Z_j - 1)$, mixer $e^{-i\beta H_B}$ with $H_B = \sum_i X_i$, initial state $|+\rangle^{\otimes n}$) are standard QAOA formulas cross-checked against the Farhi–Goldstone–Gutmann 2014 original, not idiosyncratic to this paper.

**Source PDF:** `work/paper.pdf` (arXiv 1907.02359v2, downloaded 2026-07-03).
